      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can see that 91 can be factored as follows:\n\n91 = 7 × 13\n\nNow, we can use the formula for the sum of divisors of a number. If a number has the prime factorization \\( p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\), then the sum of its divisors is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\sigma(n) = (1 + p_1 + p_1^2 + \\cdots + p_1^{e_1})(1 + p_2 + p_2^2 + \\cdots + p_2^{e_2}) \\cdots (1 + p_k + p_k^2 + \\cdots + p_k^{e_k})\n\\]\n\nFor 91, the sum of its divisors is:\n\n\\[\n\\sigma(91) = (1 + 7)(1 + 13) = 8 \\times 14 = 112\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 112.",
