      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. The prime factorization of 91 is:\n\n\\[ 91 = 7 \\times 13 \\]\n\nThe positive divisors of 91 are the numbers that can be formed by multiplying these prime factors in different combinations. They are:\n\n\\[ 1, 7, 13, 91 \\]\n\nTo find the sum of these divisors, we add them together:\n\n\\[ 1 + 7 + 13 + 91 \\]\n\nLet's perform the addition step-by-step:\n\nFirst, add 1 and 7:\n\n\\[ 1 + 7 = 8 \\]\n\nNext, add 13 to the result:\n\n\\[ 8 + 13 = 21 \\]\n\nFinally, add 91 to the result:\n\n\\[ 21 + 91 = 112 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{112}\n\\]",
